bibit-intent (0.1.24) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Add regression tests locking the MCP group partition used by the Runtime's
    three-MCP split: readonly/control/admin stay disjoint and complete, and the
    BIBIT_MCP_GROUPS filter matches the MCP ToolAnnotations boundaries.
  * Detect the Runtime's split Bibit MCP plugin members instead of the old single
    bibit-intent manifest when deciding whether postinst should install the
    per-user fallback MCP.

 -- Bianbu Agent <bianbu@spacemit.com>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:00:00 +0800

bibit-intent (0.1.23) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Expose the local intent HTTP service through FastAPI with API documentation.
  * Support client-known cancellation IDs and reject delayed cancelled requests.
  * Prevent cloud replay after permission denial or partial device execution.
  * Own the fixed local model catalog and lifecycle through the HTTP service.
  * Deliver the MCP definition only through the Runtime package's plugin and
    retire the user-home copy installs used to write, so one Bibit Intent MCP
    is loaded instead of two identical sets of tools.
  * Launch desktop applications from trusted Host workers through the user
    service manager so terminals use the desktop filesystem namespace.
  * Keep sandbox launches isolated and reject missing Host identity markers
    or failed user-service activation without silently falling back.

 -- liudecheng <decheng.liu@spacemit.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0800

bibit-intent (0.1.1) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Enable and start the three user services (bibit-intent, bibit-intent-llm,
    bibit-intent-embed) for logged-in users right after install.
  * Restart the user services on upgrade so changed unit config (model path,
    ExecStart commands) and new code take effect.
  * Enable per-user only (no global enablement) to avoid port conflicts when
    multiple users are logged in.
  * Order bibit-intent after the llm and embedding servers.

